   "id": "chat-lmsys-0005",
   "stratum": "chat",
   "source": "lmsys",
   "prompt": "Give me a list of digital products for kids that involves story telling",
   "response": "Here is a list of digital products for kids that involve storytelling, categorized by the type of experience they offer. These range from interactive narratives to tools that let kids *become* the storyteller.\n\n### 1. Interactive & Choose-Your-Own-Adventure Apps\n*These products let kids influence the plot, making them active participants in the story.*\n\n- **Luminosity (by Night Zookeeper):** A creative writing platform where kids go on adventures and write stories to \"save\" magical animals. The story evolves based on their writing prompts.\n- **Twist:** An AI-powered app where kids create illustrated stories by typing sentences. They can twist the plot by adding new characters or \"what if\" scenarios.\n- **Inklewriter (Web-based):** A free, simple tool that lets kids write and publish their own interactive \"choose-your-own-adventure\" stories with branching paths.\n- **The Foos (by CodeSpark):** While primarily a coding app, it uses storytelling to teach logic. Kids solve puzzles to advance a narrative, effectively \"writing\" the ending through code.\n\n### 2. Audio-Only Storytelling (Podcasts & Smart Speakers)\n*Great for screen-free time and imagination.*\n\n- **StoryButton (Hardware):** A small, button-shaped device that plays a short, kid-friendly audio story or song each time it's pressed. No screen, no ads.\n- **Yoto Player (Hardware + App):** A screen-free audio player that uses \"cards.\" Kids insert a card (e.g., *Harry Potter*, *Clifford*) to play a professionally narrated story. The app also offers a \"Make Your Own\" card where you can record your own voice telling a story.\n- **Podcast:** *Story Pirates* (turns real kids' stories into funny sketches), *Circle Round* (folk tales from around the world), *The Past and The Curious* (history stories with a twist).\n\n### 3. Story Creation & Animation Tools\n*Products that give kids the power to write, illustrate, and animate their own stories.*\n\n- **Toontastic 3D (by Google):** A free app that uses a \"story arc\" structure (Setup, Conflict, Challenge, Climax, Resolution). Kids design characters, move them on a 3D set, and record their voice to create a full animated cartoon.\n- **Pictory (for Kids):** An AI storyboard tool. Kids write a short story",
