   "id": "chat-lmsys-0011",
   "stratum": "chat",
   "source": "lmsys",
   "prompt": "Write for me the abstract of the following paper:\n\nTitle: Decision Transformer: Reinforcement Learning via Sequence Modeling\nAbstract:",
   "response": "**Abstract**\n\nRecent work in reinforcement learning (RL) has typically framed the problem as learning a policy or value function through interaction with an environment. In this paper, we propose a fundamentally different architecture, the Decision Transformer, which reframes RL as a sequence modeling problem. Instead of learning a policy that directly maps states to actions, we train a transformer-based model to output the desired action autoregressively, conditioned on a trajectory of past states, actions, and *returns-to-go* (the sum of future rewards). This approach allows us to leverage the powerful sequence modeling capabilities of transformers, originally developed for language, to model the joint distribution over trajectories. Empirically, the Decision Transformer matches or exceeds the performance of strong offline RL baselines on several continuous control tasks, including Atari, while also exhibiting key properties such as adaptability to different reward scales without retraining. Our work highlights the potential of sequence modeling as a unifying framework for decision-making, bridging ideas from RL and supervised learning.",
   "response_start": 27,
