   "prompt": "which 3gpp spec describe lte rlc?",
   "response": "The LTE RLC (Radio Link Control) protocol is primarily described in the following 3GPP specification:\n\n**3GPP TS 36.322** — *\"Evolved Universal Terrestrial Radio Access (E-UTRA); Radio Link Control (RLC) protocol specification\"*\n\nThis specification covers:\n- RLC architecture, including the three modes: **Transparent Mode (TM)**, **Unacknowledged Mode (UM)**, and **Acknowledged Mode (AM)**\n- RLC PDU (Protocol Data Unit) formats and structures\n- RLC functions: segmentation, reassembly, error correction, in-sequence delivery, duplicate detection, etc.\n- Procedures for data transfer, control, and status reporting\n\n**Supporting specifications:**\n- **TS 36.300** (E-UTRA and E-UTRAN Overall Description) — Provides the broader architecture context, including RLC role within Layer 2.\n- **TS 36.323** — For PDCP (Packet Data Convergence Protocol), which works closely with RLC.\n- **TS 36.331** — For RRC (Radio Resource Control) protocol, which configures RLC parameters.\n\nIf you are working with **5G NR**, the equivalent specification is **3GPP TS 38.322**.",
