   "id": "chat-lmsys-0015",
   "stratum": "chat",
   "source": "lmsys",
   "prompt": "organize this as a paragraph : \nprofiler : input profile and organisation , full name last name, username and phone number\n           info will be retrieved in all platforms \n\n3 services : data service, IA service and scraper service\n\ndata service handle the communication between interfaces ui and our scraper\n\nbrowser --- profiler service ---- data service service \nrabbitmq events handler with data as real time data.\n\nauthentification process : rabbitmq process authentification , multiple authentification layers\n\ntopic between us and ui interface : one topic, we are the responsible\n\nsection part inside UI:\n\nid 1,20,30,4  action photos\nid 5,52  action infos default latest\n\nrefresh part.\n\nminimum requirements : avatar number in real time data in search part (performance)\nservice to analyse profile and decide number of avatar to send.\n\n\nprofiler service will send the neo4j ids and depth and data service will return the data.\nafter each click in the UI we can retrieve data needed.",
   "response": "The profiler service accepts input consisting of a profile and organization details—specifically, the full name, last name, username, and phone number—and retrieves the corresponding information across all platforms. This functionality is supported by three core services: the data service, the IA service, and the scraper service. The data service manages communication between the user interface and the scraper, following a flow from the browser to the profiler service and then to the data service, with RabbitMQ event handlers facilitating real-time data processing. Authentication is handled through RabbitMQ with multiple layers of security. A single topic is established between our system and the UI interface, for which we are responsible. Within the UI, specific sections are defined: IDs 1, 20, 30, and 4 correspond to photo actions, while IDs 5 and 52 handle default info actions for the latest data. A refresh mechanism is also included. The minimum requirement is to display the avatar number in real-time data during the search phase to ensure performance, supported by a service that analyzes the profile and determines how many avatars to send. The profiler service sends Neo4j IDs and depth information to the data service, which then returns the requested data; after each click in the UI, the necessary data is retrieved accordingly.",
