   "prompt": "I have almost four hours till work, I need to shower, exercise, do homework, and then I can do some meditation/reading/planning. It's 11am now, let's make a schedule.",
   "response": "Here’s a realistic schedule that balances your tasks with breaks, starting at 11:00 AM. Since you have almost 4 hours (until ~2:50 PM, assuming work starts at 3 PM), I’ve allowed for flexibility.\n\n**11:00–11:15** – **Get ready** (change into workout clothes, prep water/snacks)  \n**11:15–11:45** – **Exercise** (30-min high-intensity or a brisk walk/jog + core; if you need longer, shift later)  \n**11:45–12:00** – **Cool down + stretch** (shower prep, grab towel)  \n**12:00–12:20** – **Shower** (quick, efficient)  \n**12:20–12:30** – **Quick snack + transition** (eat something light, set up study area)  \n**12:30–1:45** – **Homework** (75-min focused block, take a 5-min break at 1:15 if needed)  \n**1:45–2:00** – **Snack/water break + stretch**  \n**2:00–2:45** – **Meditation/Reading/Planning** (use remaining time however you like; even 15–20 mins helps)  \n**2:45–2:55** – **Final prep** (pack bag, review to-do list, get ready for work)  \n**2:55** – **Head out**\n\n**Adjust if needed:**  \n- If exercise is longer, shorten homework or meditation.  \n- If homework is heavy, extend it and reduce meditation to 15 min.  \n- Use the final 10 minutes for mindfulness, even if it’s just deep breathing.\n\n**Tip:** Set a timer for each block to stay on track. You’ve got this—plenty of time!",
