   "prompt": "icao annex 4 amendment 81 chsmges summaries",
   "response": "Here is a summary of the key changes introduced by **ICAO Annex 4 (Aeronautical Charts)** , **Amendment 81**.\n\n**Context:** This amendment is largely driven by the implementation of **AIM (Aeronautical Information Management)** requirements, the transition from paper-centric to digital (electronic) AIPs (eAIPs), and harmonization with the **AIS to AIM** roadmap.\n\n**Effective Date:** Typically, amendments become applicable 6 months after adoption (e.g., November 2024 / March 2025). You should verify the exact applicability date against the ICAO State Letter.\n\n**Core Summary of Changes (AMENDMENT 81):**\n\n### 1. General / Structure Changes\n- **Introduction of EAD (Electronic Aeronautical Data):** The amendment removes specific paper publication requirements (e.g., fixed page layouts for the AIP) to allow for the **Electronic AIP (eAIP)** .\n- **Data Set Specifications:** The biggest change is the addition of **specifications for Chart Data Sets** (not just the visual chart). This aligns with the **Aeronautical Data Process (ADP)** and **Data Set** concepts in Annex 15.\n- **New Standard (SARPs) for Electronic Charts:** While previously Annex 4 assumed printed charts (with legend and symbology), Amendment 81 introduces standards for **digital display of charts** on screens (e.g., for EFBs, Cockpit displays).\n\n### 2. Specific Chapters / Chart Changes\n\n**Chapter 2 (General Requirements):**\n- **Portrayal rules** for digital data exchange are now mandatory.\n- **Metadata requirements** for charts (digital source, currency, resolution) are introduced.\n- **Symbology:** Updated to include symbols for **GBAS (Ground-Based Augmentation System)** , **ADS-B (Automatic Dependent Surveillance-Broadcast)** ground stations, and **Space-Based ADS-B** (e.g., Aireon).\n\n**Chapter 4 (Aerodrome Obstacle Chart - ICAO Type A & B):**\n- **Enhanced obstacle symbols:** New symbology for groups of obstacles and man-made obstacles (e.g., wind turbines, crane symbols) that are more precise for digital rendering.\n- **Digital Layer:** States can now provide these charts as digital layers (Geo-referenced TIFF/S-57 style) rather than just physical paper prints.\n\n**Chapter 6 (Instrument Approach Charts (IAC)):**\n- **RNAV/",
