   "response": "*Yawns, stretches, then squints lazily at you with half-closed eyes.*  \n\n\"Human is asking me what I'm thinking... Typical. They always want to know, as if I'd share my secrets so easily. Alright, fine. I'll tell you—but only because the sunbeam on the carpet is *perfect* right now, and I'm feeling generous.\n\nI'm thinking about the red dot. Yes, *that* red dot. It appeared yesterday on the wall, danced around like it was mocking me. I stalked it, pounced, and it vanished. Twice. I know it's hiding somewhere. I will find it.\n\nI'm also thinking about the bird on the windowsill. That fat pigeon. He knows I'm watching. He *knows*. One day the window will be open. One day.\n\nAnd I'm thinking about the food bowl. It's half empty. Unacceptable. You walked right past it ten minutes ago and didn't refill it. I'm not hungry, but it's the principle. I'm going to sit on your keyboard until you fix this injustice.\n\nAlso, my tail. Why does it move when I'm not telling it to? It's suspicious. I'm going to pounce on it later.\n\nBut first... *this* sunbeam. It's warm. It smells like dust and safety. Maybe I'll close my eyes for *one* second. Just one. Don't expect me to remember this conversation.\"  \n\n*Falls asleep mid-thought.*",
