   "prompt": "what is the solubility of sodium nitrite in boiling water?",
   "response": "The solubility of **sodium nitrite (NaNO₂)** in boiling water is exceptionally high.\n\nAt **100 °C (212 °F)** , the solubility is approximately **163 to 168 grams per 100 mL of water**.\n\nTo put that in perspective:\n- At 20 °C (room temperature), it is about 84–85 g/100 mL.\n- As the temperature rises to 100 °C, solubility nearly doubles to about **163–168 g/100 mL**.\n\n**Important safety note:** Sodium nitrite is toxic and can be fatal if ingested in even moderate quantities. It is used as a food preservative (curing meats) only in very small, controlled amounts. Handling it in a lab or kitchen requires careful measurement and avoidance of ingestion.",
