   "stratum": "chat",
   "source": "lmsys",
   "prompt": "Show me how to implement a toy version of a relational database. Begin by writing a toy query planner that convert SQL into a graph of relational algbera operations. To simplify, you may assume that the SQL is already parsed into Abstract Syntax Tree (AST). You also only need to implement basic \"select\" that may have some columns only, with \"where\" clause, but no sort by or pagination.",
   "response": "I'll show you how to implement a toy relational database with a query planner. Let's build this step by step.\n\n## 1. First, let's define our data types\n\n```haskell\n-- Types.hs\nmodule Types where\n\n-- Abstract Syntax Tree for our simplified SQL\ndata SQL = Select \n    { columns :: [ColumnExpr]      -- SELECT clause\n    , table :: TableName            -- FROM clause\n    , whereClause :: Maybe Expr    -- WHERE clause\n    } deriving (Show, Eq)\n\ntype ColumnExpr = String  -- can be \"name\", \"age\", or \"*\"\ntype TableName = String\n\n-- Simple expression parser\ndata Expr\n    = Column String\n    | Value ValueType\n    | BinOp Op Expr Expr\n    deriving (Show, Eq)\n\ndata Op = Eq | Neq | Gt | Lt | Gte | Lte\n    deriving (Show, Eq)\n\ndata ValueType\n    = IntVal Int\n    | StringVal String\n    | BoolVal Bool\n    deriving (Show, Eq)\n```\n\n## 2. Define Relational Algebra Operations\n\n```haskell\n-- RelAlgebra.hs\nmodule RelAlgebra where\nimport Types\n\n-- Relational Algebra Operations\ndata RelAlgNode\n    = Scan TableName          -- Table scan\n    | Project [ColumnExpr]    -- Projection (SELECT columns)\n    | SelectOp Expr           -- Selection (WHERE clause)\n    | Rename TableName        -- Rename operation\n    deriving (Show, Eq)\n\n-- Query Plan is a tree of relational algebra operations\ntype QueryPlan = RelAlgOp\n\n-- Combined operations for easier handling\ndata RelAlgOp\n    = LeafOperation RelAlgNode\n    | UnaryOperation RelAlgNode RelAlgOp\n    deriving (Show, Eq)\n```\n\n## 3. Implement the Query Planner\n\n```haskell\n-- QueryPlanner.hs\nmodule QueryPlanner where\nimport Types\nimport RelAlgebra\n\n-- Main planner function\nplanQuery :: SQL -> QueryPlan\nplanQuery (Select cols table whereClause) =\n    case whereClause of\n        Nothing -> \n            -- Simple SELECT without WHERE\n            projectOperation $ scanOperation table cols\n        Just expr ->\n            -- SELECT with WHERE clause\n            unifyOperations table cols expr\n\n-- Create a scan operation\nscanOperation :: TableName -> [ColumnExpr] -> QueryPlan\nscan",
